Adaptations replace framework imports with local pure helpers/structural types.
Bounded caches are retained. Missing timezone throws instead of using the host
timezone. Cron keeps first-fold resolution; the offsetless-at caller opts into
ambiguity rejection. The public at grammar retains accepted second precision.
Raw historical negative instants are filtered from the public nonnegative domain.
No timer/callback is passed to Croner.
R8's definition validation rejects invalid explicit widths instead of silently
coercing them. Cron matching uses exact croner@10.0.1; no custom cron parser or
host/store/executor import is introduced. Per-file SHA256/Git blob identifiers
and adaptations are in docs/cron-schedule/import-proof.json. Checksum-verified
reference snapshots and generate-fixtures.mjs retain MIT notices and execute
only pure helper extracts, never host/service runtime modules.
decisions.ts is new Apache-2.0 policy code. The host's license is unchanged.
